$, where $\\beta \\ge 0$ is a real number with $\\beta < \\alpha$. Suppose that $b_n \\neq 0$ for all sufficiently large $n$, that $b_{n-1} / b_n \\to \\beta$ as $n \\to \\infty$, and that $A(\\beta) \\neq 0$. Then the coefficients…","route":"../roadmap/Analysis/asymptotic-analysis/bender-s-lemma/index.html#bender-product-coefficient-asymptotic"}],"result_edges":[["Analysis/asymptotic-analysis/bender-s-lemma/bender-product-coefficient-asymptotic","Analysis/asymptotic-analysis/bender-s-lemma/bender-product-coefficient-asymptotic-ge",0,1]],"boundary_edges":[],"outside":[]},"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures":{"part":{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures","title":"Dimension functions for Hausdorff measures","results":7,"status":{"fully_proved":7},"parts":0,"api":[],"api_total":0,"imports_total":0,"file":"98.json"},"path":[["region:Analysis & Probability","Analysis & Probability"],["MeasureTheory","Measure Theory"],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory","Geometric measure theory"],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures","Dimension functions for Hausdorff measures"]],"children":[],"edges":[],"links":{"uses":[],"uses_total":0,"used_by":[],"used_by_total":0},"results":[{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/hausdorff-dimension-function","title":"Hausdorff dimension function","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Structure","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction","summary":"A Hausdorff dimension function (gauge) is a continuous, non-decreasing function $\\psi : [0,\\infty) \\to [0,\\infty)$ with $\\psi(0) = 0$ and $\\psi(r) > 0$ for every $r > 0$. In particular $\\psi(r) \\to 0$ as $r \\to 0^+$.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#hausdorff-dimension-function"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/continuous","title":"Continuity of a Hausdorff dimension function","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.continuous","summary":"Every Hausdorff dimension function $\\psi : [0,\\infty) \\to [0,\\infty)$ is continuous.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#continuous"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/monotone","title":"Monotonicity of a Hausdorff dimension function","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.monotone","summary":"Every Hausdorff dimension function $\\psi : [0,\\infty) \\to [0,\\infty)$ is non-decreasing: if $r \\le s$ then $\\psi(r) \\le \\psi(s)$.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#monotone"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-zero","title":"A Hausdorff dimension function vanishes at zero","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.map_zero","summary":"Every Hausdorff dimension function $\\psi$ satisfies $\\psi(0) = 0$.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#map-zero"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-pos","title":"A Hausdorff dimension function is positive at positive radii","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.map_pos","summary":"If $\\psi$ is a Hausdorff dimension function and $r > 0$ is a real number, then $\\psi(r) > 0$.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#map-pos"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-eq-zero-iff","title":"A Hausdorff dimension function vanishes only at zero","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.map_eq_zero_iff","summary":"If $\\psi$ is a Hausdorff dimension function and $r \\ge 0$, then $\\psi(r) = 0$ if and only if $r = 0$.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#map-eq-zero-iff"},{"id":"MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/tendsto-zero","title":"A Hausdorff dimension function tends to zero at zero","status":"fully_proved","caption":"Theorem","lean":"HausdorffDimensionFunction.tendsto_zero","summary":"Every Hausdorff dimension function $\\psi$ satisfies $\\psi(r) \\to 0$ as $r \\to 0^+$, that is, as $r$ tends to $0$ through positive values.","route":"../roadmap/MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/index.html#tendsto-zero"}],"result_edges":[["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/tendsto-zero","MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/continuous",0,1],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/continuous","MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/hausdorff-dimension-function",1,0],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-eq-zero-iff","MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/hausdorff-dimension-function",1,0],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-pos","MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/hausdorff-dimension-function",1,0],["MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/map-zero","MeasureTheory/geometric-measure-theory/dimension-functions-for-hausdorff-measures/hausdorff-dimension-function